=====================================================================
PINOUT Shows All No-Connect (NC)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
The VIEW/PINOUT option in the menu works directly from your design
file. If you are floating signals in the Pin/Node declaration section
of your design file these will be displayed as NC on the pinout
diagram. A list of all floating signals is given if you scroll to the
bottom of the display. This is a common occurrence if processing
designs for MACH devices.

To remedy this situation you must backannotate the signal placement data
from a successful design compilation to your design file. To do this execute
the following steps in the PALASM menu.

        1. Select 'RUN' option
        2. Select 'Other operations ...' option
        3. Select 'Back annotate signals ...' option
        4. Select 'Use last successful placement' option

When this task successfully completes re-try VIEW/PINOUT option.
